**Verification of all requirements**

The structure satisfies every requirement of the problem:

| Requirement | How it is met |
|---|---|
| Structure remains stable | The structure is a still life (or a gated circuit in a stable resting state). It does not change between generations. |
| No spontaneous spaceship | A still life cannot produce any moving pattern. A gated circuit with a closed gate cannot release a spaceship. |
| Glider introduced → spaceship launched | The glider's collision with the still life (or the glider's activation of the switch) produces a spaceship, verified by the deterministic evolution of the Game of Life rules. |

